1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:04,000
I can't believe Natsuki
actually has someone he likes.

2
00:00:04,100 --> 00:00:06,267
I'll always be on your side.

3
00:00:06,367 --> 00:00:07,533
Sota.

4
00:00:07,633 --> 00:00:10,633
If he wasn't my sister's boyfriend...

5
00:00:10,733 --> 00:00:11,767
Wait, a cold?

6
00:00:11,867 --> 00:00:13,667
What if he passes out?

7
00:00:13,767 --> 00:00:14,633
He might even die all
alone in his apartment.

8
00:00:14,733 --> 00:00:15,400
So-chan.

9
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:16,500
Na-chan?

10
00:00:17,533 --> 00:00:18,533
Thank goodness.

11
00:00:19,433 --> 00:00:24,867
Could it be... I've
actually fallen for him?

12
00:00:24,967 --> 00:00:26,367
Fallen for So-chan...

13
00:00:26,467 --> 00:00:27,467
Na-chan.

14
00:00:28,333 --> 00:00:31,767
I shouldn't have actually
fallen for someone...

15
00:00:34,967 --> 00:00:36,467
I'm such an idiot...

16
00:00:37,567 --> 00:00:39,400
I just caused him trouble.

17
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:41,467
Na-chan, wait.

18
00:00:46,100 --> 00:00:47,100
I'm sorry.

19
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:49,833
I definitely freaked him out...

20
00:00:51,133 --> 00:00:52,213
I just want to disappear...

21
00:00:57,300 --> 00:00:58,433
Rock.

22
00:00:58,833 --> 00:01:01,633
Na-chan, the cold noodles are ready!

23
00:01:03,033 --> 00:01:04,033
Coming!

24
00:01:12,633 --> 00:01:15,000
"Your Summer, My Storm"
(Episode 6)

25
00:01:17,767 --> 00:01:18,767
Here you go.

26
00:01:19,400 --> 00:01:21,033
Wow, that looks delicious.

27
00:01:31,200 --> 00:01:32,567
Here, Natsuki.

28
00:01:32,667 --> 00:01:33,667
Thanks.

29
00:01:34,067 --> 00:01:35,600
Alright, thanks for waiting.

30
00:01:36,067 --> 00:01:36,533
Well then.

31
00:01:36,633 --> 00:01:37,633
Okay.

32
00:01:37,800 --> 00:01:39,700
Let's eat.

33
00:01:40,167 --> 00:01:41,309
Wow, there's wood ear mushroom!

34
00:01:41,333 --> 00:01:43,300
It's fresh wood ear
mushroom, it's really good.

35
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:44,633
Oh, awesome!

36
00:01:44,733 --> 00:01:45,600
Let's eat.

37
00:01:45,700 --> 00:01:47,367
I put a little extra in yours, Rio.

38
00:01:47,467 --> 00:01:48,800
Yay!

39
00:01:52,533 --> 00:01:53,033
Hmm?

40
00:01:53,233 --> 00:01:53,800
Huh?

41
00:01:53,967 --> 00:01:54,533
Are you not going to eat that?

42
00:01:54,900 --> 00:01:55,900
Yeah.

43
00:01:56,067 --> 00:01:56,867
You can have it.

44
00:01:56,967 --> 00:01:59,333
Natsuki, do you not like
wood ear mushrooms?

45
00:01:59,433 --> 00:02:00,933
No, I...

46
00:02:01,033 --> 00:02:04,167
Have I really fallen for him?

47
00:02:05,433 --> 00:02:06,433
I don't like them.

48
00:02:06,833 --> 00:02:08,833
Oh no, I had no idea.

49
00:02:08,933 --> 00:02:10,367
It's not that I really hate them.

50
00:02:10,667 --> 00:02:12,667
I'm just not in the mood for them today.

51
00:02:12,767 --> 00:02:14,533
Why are you being so awkward?

52
00:02:14,633 --> 00:02:16,800
I didn't know eating mushrooms
depended on your mood.

53
00:02:18,200 --> 00:02:19,567
Well, don't mind if I do.

54
00:02:19,967 --> 00:02:21,233
Oh, I'll go pour some tea.

55
00:02:21,733 --> 00:02:23,600
Mmm, this is so good.

56
00:02:27,033 --> 00:02:28,567
I'm so glad Sota is okay.

57
00:02:29,100 --> 00:02:29,600
Huh?

58
00:02:29,700 --> 00:02:30,300
What?

59
00:02:30,400 --> 00:02:32,800
Is Sota-san over his cold?

60
00:02:32,900 --> 00:02:33,533
Yeah.

61
00:02:33,833 --> 00:02:34,967
He's fully recovered.

62
00:02:35,400 --> 00:02:36,743
He said he's going to play tennis later.

63
00:02:36,767 --> 00:02:38,667
That's great.

64
00:02:38,767 --> 00:02:40,700
After all, the mock exams are next week.

65
00:02:40,800 --> 00:02:41,800
Is it already that time?

66
00:02:41,833 --> 00:02:43,267
Tell me about it.

67
00:02:44,633 --> 00:02:47,767
Is Dad really going to look
at your mock exam scores

68
00:02:47,867 --> 00:02:49,343
before deciding if you can take
the college entrance exams?

69
00:02:49,367 --> 00:02:51,367
No problem, I've been working hard.

70
00:02:51,467 --> 00:02:53,333
Speaking of your dad...

71
00:02:53,633 --> 00:02:54,633
Hmm?

72
00:02:57,733 --> 00:03:03,100
Hey, have you guys heard anything
from your dad lately?

73
00:03:03,300 --> 00:03:04,767
Do you mean about Natsuki?

74
00:03:04,867 --> 00:03:05,867
No.

75
00:03:06,867 --> 00:03:09,500
He's been acting a bit weird lately.

76
00:03:10,367 --> 00:03:11,267
What are you looking at?

77
00:03:11,367 --> 00:03:12,467
Nothing, it's nothing.

78
00:03:12,967 --> 00:03:13,767
Right?

79
00:03:13,867 --> 00:03:16,333
I wasn't looking at anything, right, Rock?

80
00:03:16,433 --> 00:03:18,633
I just feel like he's
hiding something from me.

81
00:03:20,133 --> 00:03:21,973
You don't think he's
having an affair, do you?

82
00:03:22,500 --> 00:03:23,533
What?

83
00:03:24,267 --> 00:03:26,467
Oh, I see.

84
00:03:26,567 --> 00:03:27,567
Will that work?

85
00:03:28,267 --> 00:03:30,067
Awesome.

86
00:03:30,667 --> 00:03:31,667
Huh?

87
00:03:33,633 --> 00:03:36,700
Of course I'm looking forward to it.

88
00:03:36,800 --> 00:03:40,233
A stiff guy like him? There's
no way he'd have an affair.

89
00:03:40,333 --> 00:03:42,467
I hope you're right...

90
00:03:46,333 --> 00:03:47,200
Oh...

91
00:03:47,300 --> 00:03:48,500
Huh?

92
00:03:55,067 --> 00:03:57,167
(Sota's friend, Uesugi Ryunosuke)

93
00:04:05,833 --> 00:04:06,833
Ah!

94
00:04:10,367 --> 00:04:11,833
Nice!

95
00:04:13,500 --> 00:04:15,067
Damn it.

96
00:04:15,867 --> 00:04:16,867
I lost.

97
00:04:16,967 --> 00:04:18,800
Man, that was an easy win.

98
00:04:18,900 --> 00:04:20,133
Damn it.

99
00:04:20,467 --> 00:04:22,400
- Here you go.
- Thanks.

100
00:04:22,500 --> 00:04:23,733
It's so hot.

101
00:04:25,333 --> 00:04:26,400
What's going on?

102
00:04:27,367 --> 00:04:28,367
Huh?

103
00:04:28,900 --> 00:04:30,309
I mean, you're usually so organized, Sota.

104
00:04:30,333 --> 00:04:32,843
It's super rare for you to suddenly
ask me out to play tennis like this.

105
00:04:32,867 --> 00:04:34,467
It happens sometimes.

106
00:04:34,867 --> 00:04:36,067
Is something bothering you?

107
00:04:36,167 --> 00:04:37,367
I'm here to listen.

108
00:04:37,900 --> 00:04:39,467
Did you get a girlfriend?

109
00:04:40,333 --> 00:04:41,467
No way.

110
00:04:41,567 --> 00:04:43,033
You're acting really suspicious.

111
00:04:43,133 --> 00:04:44,573
- Alright, one more game.
- No, wait.

112
00:04:44,633 --> 00:04:45,633
Hurry up, get up.

113
00:04:45,733 --> 00:04:47,033
Huh?

114
00:04:47,467 --> 00:04:53,567
Have I really fallen for him?

115
00:04:55,433 --> 00:04:56,767
Fallen for him?

116
00:04:57,967 --> 00:04:59,333
Sukiyaki?

117
00:04:59,767 --> 00:05:01,033
Skip?

118
00:05:02,800 --> 00:05:04,067
No way.

119
00:05:05,767 --> 00:05:06,367
Natsuki.

120
00:05:06,467 --> 00:05:07,600
Wh-What?

121
00:05:08,100 --> 00:05:10,467
I washed the T-shirt I
borrowed from you. Here.

122
00:05:10,633 --> 00:05:11,633
Oh...

123
00:05:14,767 --> 00:05:15,767
Natsuki.

124
00:05:17,767 --> 00:05:18,767
Yeah?

125
00:05:22,967 --> 00:05:23,967
What is it?

126
00:05:25,667 --> 00:05:27,367
Make sure you study hard.

127
00:05:28,367 --> 00:05:29,367
I know.

128
00:05:42,600 --> 00:05:43,767
You played well.

129
00:05:43,867 --> 00:05:44,867
That's great.

130
00:05:47,033 --> 00:05:48,533
(Incoming call: Rio)

131
00:05:50,233 --> 00:05:51,233
Hello.

132
00:05:52,900 --> 00:05:53,900
Yeah...

133
00:05:54,267 --> 00:05:55,467
Oh...

134
00:05:55,833 --> 00:05:57,267
The design is great.

135
00:05:57,567 --> 00:05:59,543
The contrast with the color of
the ocean is absolutely beautiful.

136
00:05:59,567 --> 00:06:00,567
- Right?
- Yeah.

137
00:06:00,600 --> 00:06:01,333
I'll send this one to you.

138
00:06:01,433 --> 00:06:02,100
Oh, thanks.

139
00:06:02,200 --> 00:06:03,200
Yeah.

140
00:06:06,333 --> 00:06:07,333
Alright.

141
00:06:07,867 --> 00:06:09,267
Now for the main topic.

142
00:06:09,733 --> 00:06:10,433
Huh?

143
00:06:10,533 --> 00:06:11,867
What main topic?

144
00:06:11,967 --> 00:06:12,967
Well.

145
00:06:14,067 --> 00:06:15,333
It's about yesterday.

146
00:06:15,800 --> 00:06:16,800
Huh?

147
00:06:18,100 --> 00:06:19,367
Yesterday?

148
00:06:21,367 --> 00:06:23,600
After I got off work,

149
00:06:24,133 --> 00:06:27,867
I went to your apartment
building to see you.

150
00:06:28,100 --> 00:06:29,100
What?

151
00:06:30,667 --> 00:06:32,233
Just as I was about to go in,

152
00:06:33,067 --> 00:06:35,467
I saw Natsuki run out crying.

153
00:06:36,033 --> 00:06:37,033
Na-chan.

154
00:06:37,233 --> 00:06:39,200
You chased after him, right?

155
00:06:39,300 --> 00:06:43,167
But it didn't seem like you
really wanted to catch him.

156
00:06:46,467 --> 00:06:49,033
That guy has been a
crybaby since we were kids.

157
00:06:49,867 --> 00:06:51,867
He cries over everything.

158
00:06:52,433 --> 00:06:54,167
So it's not exactly unusual.

159
00:06:55,967 --> 00:07:00,067
But... the vibe just felt really off.

160
00:07:01,233 --> 00:07:03,533
So I didn't call out to you guys.

161
00:07:04,433 --> 00:07:07,467
I see... so that's what happened.

162
00:07:09,233 --> 00:07:11,533
I was going to ask Natsuki about it today,

163
00:07:12,233 --> 00:07:14,933
but I just couldn't
bring myself to do it...

164
00:07:15,733 --> 00:07:18,833
So I figured I'd just ask you instead.

165
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:21,067
I see.

166
00:07:21,733 --> 00:07:24,033
Though it feels a bit
weird to say it like that.

167
00:07:28,267 --> 00:07:29,867
Did something happen?

168
00:07:38,600 --> 00:07:39,967
Actually...

169
00:07:41,500 --> 00:07:44,100
I confessed on impulse.
What should I do now?

170
00:07:45,533 --> 00:07:48,933
Send a brief apology text
within two hours.

171
00:07:49,033 --> 00:07:50,700
It's way past that!

172
00:07:50,800 --> 00:07:51,633
What else?

173
00:07:51,733 --> 00:07:53,833
Keep your distance for a while...

174
00:07:53,933 --> 00:07:55,433
He's coming over soon!

175
00:07:55,533 --> 00:07:56,667
What do I do, Rock?

176
00:07:56,767 --> 00:07:57,867
Save me!

177
00:08:03,333 --> 00:08:04,700
I'm home.

178
00:08:05,867 --> 00:08:06,633
It's my sister.

179
00:08:06,733 --> 00:08:09,200
Rock, I'm home.

180
00:08:09,800 --> 00:08:11,000
Excuse me.

181
00:08:13,567 --> 00:08:15,400
P-Please come in.

182
00:08:15,500 --> 00:08:17,000
Oh, Natsuki.

183
00:08:17,400 --> 00:08:18,967
Seeing Sota like this,

184
00:08:19,067 --> 00:08:20,307
it feels pretty awkward, right?

185
00:08:21,433 --> 00:08:22,667
Huh?

186
00:08:22,767 --> 00:08:23,967
I heard all about it.

187
00:08:24,300 --> 00:08:26,000
About yesterday.

188
00:08:26,867 --> 00:08:28,300
What about yesterday?

189
00:08:29,333 --> 00:08:31,900
I saw everything.

190
00:08:32,867 --> 00:08:36,300
I saw Natsuki run out
of Sota's place crying.

191
00:08:37,167 --> 00:08:38,167
What?

192
00:08:38,900 --> 00:08:41,167
I was really worried,

193
00:08:41,600 --> 00:08:43,100
so I went and asked Sota.

194
00:08:44,967 --> 00:08:46,267
And he said...

195
00:08:53,533 --> 00:08:55,833
He said you lost an
arm-wrestling match to him,

196
00:08:55,933 --> 00:08:57,813
and you were so frustrated
you ran home crying.

197
00:09:01,867 --> 00:09:04,700
You're not a kindergartener.

198
00:09:04,933 --> 00:09:08,200
Um... sorry for bringing it up.

199
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:10,133
It's fine.

200
00:09:10,567 --> 00:09:13,033
I was worried you guys had a fight.

201
00:09:14,367 --> 00:09:15,567
Um... sorry.

202
00:09:15,667 --> 00:09:18,333
But since that's how it is, it's fine.

203
00:09:18,433 --> 00:09:19,200
Yeah.

204
00:09:19,300 --> 00:09:20,300
Oh, right.

205
00:09:20,467 --> 00:09:23,109
The pudding I was going to bring
you yesterday when you were sick...

206
00:09:23,133 --> 00:09:25,109
I put it in the fridge. Let's
have it for a snack later.

207
00:09:25,133 --> 00:09:26,133
Thanks.

208
00:09:35,167 --> 00:09:36,000
Thank you.

209
00:09:36,100 --> 00:09:37,100
You really saved me.

210
00:09:39,467 --> 00:09:40,733
Even if it was just a joke...

211
00:09:41,800 --> 00:09:45,933
If my sister found out
I confessed to So-chan...

212
00:09:47,567 --> 00:09:52,367
She'd either yell at me or laugh at
me forever. It would be a total disaster.

213
00:09:55,433 --> 00:09:57,833
So... it was just a joke.

214
00:09:58,567 --> 00:09:59,567
Of course.

215
00:10:00,933 --> 00:10:01,933
I see...

216
00:10:03,467 --> 00:10:04,467
Goes without saying.

217
00:10:08,900 --> 00:10:09,900
Right...

218
00:10:11,667 --> 00:10:13,833
Well... let's get started.

219
00:10:13,933 --> 00:10:14,933
Yeah.

220
00:10:15,067 --> 00:10:16,067
I'm counting on you.

221
00:10:16,133 --> 00:10:17,133
Okay.

222
00:10:27,067 --> 00:10:29,433
I think I fooled him...?

223
00:10:38,600 --> 00:10:42,600
Maybe it's better to just ask him directly?

224
00:10:43,733 --> 00:10:44,733
Huh?

225
00:10:44,767 --> 00:10:45,767
Ask what?

226
00:10:47,133 --> 00:10:48,400
About your dad.

227
00:10:48,700 --> 00:10:51,220
I want to ask him straight up if
he's hiding something from me.

228
00:10:51,333 --> 00:10:52,567
Ah...

229
00:10:53,200 --> 00:10:54,600
I wonder.

230
00:11:02,467 --> 00:11:05,333
Na-chan, you're amazing! 90 points!

231
00:11:05,433 --> 00:11:06,167
Really?

232
00:11:06,267 --> 00:11:07,267
Yeah.

233
00:11:07,900 --> 00:11:10,167
Are you starting to find
the questions easier?

234
00:11:11,867 --> 00:11:13,967
Rather than them getting easier...

235
00:11:14,933 --> 00:11:17,043
It's more like I'm starting to
understand how to solve them.

236
00:11:17,067 --> 00:11:19,333
That means they're getting easier!

237
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:21,167
I guess so.

238
00:11:21,267 --> 00:11:23,133
In that case...

239
00:11:23,233 --> 00:11:24,033
Here are 10 tickets.

240
00:11:24,133 --> 00:11:24,933
Huh?

241
00:11:25,033 --> 00:11:25,933
This many?

242
00:11:26,033 --> 00:11:28,067
Because you've really improved a lot.

243
00:11:28,167 --> 00:11:30,600
At first, you said you
couldn't do a single question.

244
00:11:31,067 --> 00:11:32,067
Well...

245
00:11:32,233 --> 00:11:33,933
That's true.

246
00:11:34,033 --> 00:11:35,376
Let's take a picture to celebrate.

247
00:11:35,400 --> 00:11:35,867
Huh?

248
00:11:35,967 --> 00:11:36,867
- Come on.
- Hold on.

249
00:11:36,967 --> 00:11:37,833
Alright, say cheese!

250
00:11:37,933 --> 00:11:39,400
Stop, this is embarrassing.

251
00:11:39,500 --> 00:11:41,220
What's the big deal? It's for the memories.

252
00:11:43,233 --> 00:11:44,467
No way...

253
00:11:44,967 --> 00:11:47,467
I'm never going to like anyone
or fall in love ever again.

254
00:11:47,867 --> 00:11:49,267
How many tickets have you saved up?

255
00:11:50,433 --> 00:11:51,433
Ah.

256
00:11:51,867 --> 00:11:53,133
I got 10 this time, right?

257
00:11:53,233 --> 00:11:54,233
Yeah.

258
00:11:54,333 --> 00:11:57,133
I had 8 before.

259
00:11:57,233 --> 00:11:57,900
So that makes 18.

260
00:11:58,000 --> 00:11:59,800
You already have that many?

261
00:11:59,900 --> 00:12:00,433
Yeah.

262
00:12:00,533 --> 00:12:04,100
By the way, if I save up 10,
wasn't there supposed to be a reward?

263
00:12:04,200 --> 00:12:06,433
Oh, sorry.

264
00:12:06,933 --> 00:12:09,067
I haven't figured out what to give you yet.

265
00:12:09,800 --> 00:12:12,167
Can we change it to when you save up 20?

266
00:12:13,467 --> 00:12:15,067
Yeah, sure.

267
00:12:15,533 --> 00:12:17,373
Let me know when you
figure out what you want.

268
00:12:18,967 --> 00:12:19,967
Okay.

269
00:12:22,133 --> 00:12:23,633
Good luck on your mock exam.

270
00:12:24,267 --> 00:12:25,267
Yeah.

271
00:12:25,367 --> 00:12:26,700
No problem, you've got this.

272
00:12:26,800 --> 00:12:28,500
Because you're a different Na-chan now.

273
00:12:29,133 --> 00:12:30,133
Yeah.

274
00:12:30,300 --> 00:12:31,967
- Bye, Rio.
- Bye.

275
00:12:34,567 --> 00:12:35,633
I'll do my best.

276
00:12:36,533 --> 00:12:38,533
Well... good night.

277
00:12:39,467 --> 00:12:40,800
Good night.

278
00:13:03,200 --> 00:13:04,200
Huh?

279
00:13:04,567 --> 00:13:05,733
What do you mean?

280
00:13:06,233 --> 00:13:09,500
I don't even know who it is,
so it's hard for me to say anything.

281
00:13:10,267 --> 00:13:11,867
Fair enough.

282
00:13:13,300 --> 00:13:15,233
But hey, do you remember?

283
00:13:15,333 --> 00:13:15,867
Hmm?

284
00:13:16,267 --> 00:13:18,167
When I got dumped by my ex...

285
00:13:18,633 --> 00:13:22,767
Rio, you didn't ask anything
and just stayed with me all night, right?

286
00:13:22,867 --> 00:13:24,933
Oh, that did happen.

287
00:13:26,167 --> 00:13:29,300
I was really happy back then.

288
00:13:29,933 --> 00:13:30,667
Really?

289
00:13:30,767 --> 00:13:31,767
Yeah.

290
00:13:32,433 --> 00:13:34,167
When people are feeling vulnerable...

291
00:13:34,800 --> 00:13:38,867
Whether someone listens to you or not...

292
00:13:38,967 --> 00:13:41,500
doesn't really matter at all.

293
00:13:42,567 --> 00:13:46,167
Just having someone on
your side stay with you...

294
00:13:46,567 --> 00:13:48,327
I think that's what
brings the most comfort.

295
00:13:52,533 --> 00:13:53,533
I see.

296
00:14:01,800 --> 00:14:02,800
Natsuki.

297
00:14:03,067 --> 00:14:05,333
Let me come walk Rock with you.

298
00:14:05,867 --> 00:14:07,167
Huh? Why the sudden interest?

299
00:14:07,267 --> 00:14:08,600
What's the big deal?

300
00:14:09,267 --> 00:14:10,367
Right, Rock?

301
00:14:11,667 --> 00:14:12,667
Yeah.

302
00:14:19,333 --> 00:14:21,033
Rock is in a great mood today.

303
00:14:22,967 --> 00:14:23,967
Oh...

304
00:14:26,567 --> 00:14:27,567
Natsuki.

305
00:14:28,033 --> 00:14:29,033
What is it?

306
00:14:30,267 --> 00:14:31,733
You like him, don't you?

307
00:14:31,833 --> 00:14:32,833
Like what?

308
00:14:34,133 --> 00:14:35,133
Sota.

309
00:14:37,667 --> 00:14:38,667
Huh?

310
00:14:47,967 --> 00:14:50,133
Did my sister find out?

311
00:14:52,767 --> 00:14:55,833
Why would I ever like So-chan?

312
00:14:57,133 --> 00:14:58,133
Why not?

313
00:15:00,267 --> 00:15:01,267
Because...

314
00:15:02,800 --> 00:15:03,867
So-chan is...

315
00:15:05,167 --> 00:15:06,300
He's a guy?

316
00:15:13,033 --> 00:15:15,353
I didn't know you cared about
that kind of thing, Natsuki.

317
00:15:16,400 --> 00:15:18,200
Normally, people would care, right?

318
00:15:20,667 --> 00:15:22,400
Normally, huh...

319
00:15:28,700 --> 00:15:30,433
It's really no big deal.

320
00:15:32,400 --> 00:15:34,967
After all, Sota is such a great guy.

321
00:15:39,567 --> 00:15:42,200
Even... if that's true...

322
00:15:45,467 --> 00:15:46,467
But...

323
00:15:47,833 --> 00:15:48,833
But what?

324
00:15:52,333 --> 00:15:53,333
I...

325
00:15:54,367 --> 00:15:57,367
I would never fall for
my sister's boyfriend.

326
00:15:58,800 --> 00:15:59,800
Huh?

327
00:16:01,533 --> 00:16:03,933
Who are you calling my "boyfriend"?

328
00:16:04,367 --> 00:16:05,067
Sota, obviously.

329
00:16:05,167 --> 00:16:05,933
Huh?

330
00:16:06,033 --> 00:16:06,533
Huh?

331
00:16:06,867 --> 00:16:08,067
Uh, no.

332
00:16:09,433 --> 00:16:10,467
What do you mean, no?

333
00:16:10,567 --> 00:16:11,567
Uh...

334
00:16:11,833 --> 00:16:13,633
Sota isn't my boyfriend.

335
00:16:14,800 --> 00:16:15,300
What?

336
00:16:15,400 --> 00:16:16,400
Huh?

337
00:16:16,733 --> 00:16:18,333
Wait, no.

338
00:16:18,533 --> 00:16:20,109
Did you think we were
dating this whole time?

339
00:16:20,133 --> 00:16:21,567
But you literally said it!

340
00:16:21,667 --> 00:16:23,100
This is Kobayakawa Sota.

341
00:16:23,200 --> 00:16:24,200
My boyfriend.

342
00:16:24,300 --> 00:16:25,367
Boy-friend.

343
00:16:26,100 --> 00:16:28,300
He's my best guy friend!

344
00:16:28,400 --> 00:16:29,809
But you put your arm
around him and hug him!

345
00:16:29,833 --> 00:16:31,400
I do that to you too, don't I?

346
00:16:31,500 --> 00:16:33,243
And every time you
go out, you call it a date!

347
00:16:33,267 --> 00:16:36,900
Whenever it's just two people going out,
I call it a date no matter who it is.

348
00:16:37,533 --> 00:16:38,533
Huh?

349
00:16:38,933 --> 00:16:39,933
No way.

350
00:16:40,167 --> 00:16:41,067
But...

351
00:16:41,167 --> 00:16:43,000
Besides, Sota has never said...

352
00:16:43,100 --> 00:16:45,767
that I'm his girlfriend or lover, right?

353
00:16:48,033 --> 00:16:49,067
Well...

354
00:16:50,067 --> 00:16:52,233
Now that you mention it... I guess not.

355
00:16:52,733 --> 00:16:53,767
Exactly.

356
00:16:54,767 --> 00:16:55,767
Huh?

357
00:16:56,700 --> 00:16:59,200
But Mom and Dad think
Sota is your boyfriend too!

358
00:16:59,300 --> 00:17:00,300
Seriously?

359
00:17:00,633 --> 00:17:02,473
I'd better clear that up
with them right away.

360
00:17:03,833 --> 00:17:04,833
Huh?

361
00:17:05,833 --> 00:17:08,533
He's really not your boyfriend?

362
00:17:08,967 --> 00:17:10,333
No, he's not!

363
00:17:12,867 --> 00:17:13,867
What the heck...

364
00:17:15,067 --> 00:17:17,000
You really thought he was my boyfriend.

365
00:17:17,100 --> 00:17:18,500
You should've just asked me sooner.

366
00:17:18,533 --> 00:17:19,543
How could I possibly
ask something like that?

367
00:17:19,567 --> 00:17:20,567
Ah.

368
00:17:21,500 --> 00:17:23,600
So that's why you went to Ryo for advice.

369
00:17:23,700 --> 00:17:27,100
Saying someone fell for
a close person's boyfriend.

370
00:17:27,767 --> 00:17:31,267
Don't tell me that "close person"
was actually me?

371
00:17:33,867 --> 00:17:36,333
Oh wow, it was me all along.

372
00:17:39,433 --> 00:17:40,700
Stop laughing!

373
00:17:41,600 --> 00:17:42,733
Sorry.

374
00:17:43,567 --> 00:17:44,567
Rock.

375
00:17:46,667 --> 00:17:48,476
Thank goodness it was
just a misunderstanding.

376
00:17:48,500 --> 00:17:50,600
If you had actually
fallen for my boyfriend...

377
00:17:50,700 --> 00:17:52,433
that would've been pure hell.

378
00:17:53,167 --> 00:17:54,600
What do you mean, hell?

379
00:17:55,667 --> 00:17:57,033
Come on.

380
00:17:57,133 --> 00:17:58,133
Go.

381
00:17:58,500 --> 00:17:59,500
Go on.

382
00:18:01,233 --> 00:18:04,300
So he's not her boyfriend...

383
00:18:09,800 --> 00:18:12,733
Do I really like him?

384
00:18:12,833 --> 00:18:14,000
Like So-chan...

385
00:18:14,100 --> 00:18:16,500
So... it was just a joke.

386
00:18:16,800 --> 00:18:17,800
Of course.

387
00:18:27,700 --> 00:18:31,067
You didn't buy the
arm-wrestling excuse, did you?

388
00:18:32,767 --> 00:18:33,767
Yeah.

389
00:18:35,233 --> 00:18:36,233
But...

390
00:18:36,867 --> 00:18:39,333
Since Sota wanted to hide it...

391
00:18:39,900 --> 00:18:42,433
I had no choice but to play along.

392
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:48,000
I see.

393
00:18:48,667 --> 00:18:50,067
I also hesitated...

394
00:18:51,500 --> 00:18:53,533
Whether to keep pretending...

395
00:18:55,433 --> 00:18:56,833
that I didn't know about it.

396
00:19:00,833 --> 00:19:04,300
You already told Sota...

397
00:19:05,567 --> 00:19:07,167
that you like him, right?

398
00:19:14,633 --> 00:19:16,400
But he didn't accept it?

399
00:19:31,267 --> 00:19:33,700
I really can't hide
anything from you, can I?

400
00:19:34,867 --> 00:19:36,100
Goes without saying.

401
00:19:39,767 --> 00:19:41,167
What did Sota say?

402
00:19:47,400 --> 00:19:48,500
He said he's sorry...

403
00:19:52,767 --> 00:19:54,833
Sorry, huh...

404
00:19:56,033 --> 00:19:58,267
Do you think he looks down on me?

405
00:19:59,633 --> 00:20:00,733
Thinks I'm gross.

406
00:20:00,833 --> 00:20:01,833
No way.

407
00:20:04,133 --> 00:20:06,233
Sota isn't like that.

408
00:20:11,833 --> 00:20:13,167
Besides, Natsuki,

409
00:20:14,400 --> 00:20:21,100
you didn't do anything to be ashamed of.

410
00:20:27,133 --> 00:20:28,033
You think so...?

411
00:20:28,133 --> 00:20:29,133
Yeah.

412
00:20:43,300 --> 00:20:44,533
I'm heading out.

413
00:20:45,033 --> 00:20:46,033
Shoot.

414
00:20:46,067 --> 00:20:46,867
Oh.

415
00:20:46,967 --> 00:20:47,967
Sorry.

416
00:20:48,033 --> 00:20:49,300
I'm really sorry.

417
00:20:49,400 --> 00:20:52,000
(3rd National Mock Exam)
Why am I so nervous for just a mock exam?

418
00:20:52,633 --> 00:20:53,767
Tell me about it.

419
00:20:53,867 --> 00:20:54,987
But isn't that a good thing?

420
00:20:55,067 --> 00:20:57,267
That tutor really boosted
your confidence, right?

421
00:20:58,267 --> 00:20:59,633
Who knows.

422
00:20:59,733 --> 00:21:00,733
Found my seat.

423
00:21:08,900 --> 00:21:10,900
(Truly falling for someone)

424
00:21:25,100 --> 00:21:26,100
Honey.

425
00:21:26,700 --> 00:21:28,800
Um... this year's...

426
00:21:28,900 --> 00:21:32,267
Natsuki should still be taking
his exam right now, right?

427
00:21:33,033 --> 00:21:34,633
Yeah...

428
00:21:35,033 --> 00:21:37,067
Though I think he'll do fine.

429
00:21:40,100 --> 00:21:41,733
If he really improves,

430
00:21:42,033 --> 00:21:44,000
we'll have to properly thank his tutor.

431
00:21:47,700 --> 00:21:49,100
Yeah...

432
00:21:50,333 --> 00:21:54,800
You already told Sota
that you like him, right?

433
00:21:57,100 --> 00:21:59,133
But he didn't accept it?

434
00:21:59,433 --> 00:22:01,367
What did Sota say?

435
00:22:01,467 --> 00:22:02,867
He said he's sorry...

436
00:22:02,967 --> 00:22:04,700
Sorry, huh...

437
00:22:06,933 --> 00:22:07,933
What's wrong?

438
00:22:09,267 --> 00:22:10,300
Nothing.

439
00:22:10,400 --> 00:22:11,400
It's nothing.

440
00:22:11,833 --> 00:22:12,833
I see.

441
00:22:13,767 --> 00:22:15,367
By the way,

442
00:22:16,700 --> 00:22:17,700
Honey.

443
00:22:18,533 --> 00:22:20,900
Are you hiding something from me?

444
00:22:21,567 --> 00:22:24,100
You've been acting weird lately.

445
00:22:25,933 --> 00:22:30,700
"Are you free tonight?"

446
00:22:40,567 --> 00:22:42,033
It's over.

447
00:22:44,533 --> 00:22:45,933
What's wrong?

448
00:22:46,167 --> 00:22:47,167
I totally bombed it.

449
00:22:48,733 --> 00:22:49,800
You're tired, right?

450
00:22:50,300 --> 00:22:52,967
Ah, let's go eat at Kazu-kun's place.

451
00:22:53,067 --> 00:22:55,133
Sure, I want some yurinchi.

452
00:22:56,167 --> 00:22:59,133
(New message from Kobayakawa Sota)

453
00:23:03,700 --> 00:23:05,400
After your mock exam,

454
00:23:05,500 --> 00:23:07,200
I want to have a proper talk with you.

455
00:23:13,433 --> 00:23:16,933
I think I'm really getting dumped.

456
00:23:18,100 --> 00:23:20,833
(This drama is purely fictional)

457
00:23:21,000 --> 00:23:21,634
(Next Episode)

458
00:23:21,667 --> 00:23:23,476
(What is Sota's past and true feelings?)
Sorry for putting you in a tough spot.

459
00:23:23,500 --> 00:23:26,900
I'm not good at romance,
where there are no right answers.

460
00:23:27,000 --> 00:23:27,800
Did I scare you?

461
00:23:27,900 --> 00:23:28,467
Yeah.

462
00:23:28,567 --> 00:23:30,366
(Ominous signs, a major event at home)
Tell me what I should do.

463
00:23:30,367 --> 00:23:33,367
Because it looks like
you've really fallen for him.

464
00:23:33,467 --> 00:23:38,533
(The more you care, the more your true
feelings pass each other by) I'm not joking.
